    "SPARSE (~20% in last 30d): gpu_model, bottleneck_dominant, driver_version, kernel_version — included in table only (bar charts would render confusing empty bars)",
    "Compare dashboard concept: pick 2 sessions via ctrl-session multi-select; all panels filter to those sessions and present them side-by-side as bars on a categorical x-axis (terms over session_id).",
    "9 panels: 2 filter controls (ctrl-session, ctrl-game) + 4 KPI bars (avg_fps, low_1pct_fps, p99_frametime, stutters) + chart-fps-compare (avg + low_1pct on shared y) + chart-thermals-power (GPU+CPU temp on y, GPU power on y2 dual-axis) + table-compare (16 metric columns, 1 row per session, alphabetical).",
    "Counter rule: stutter_count and total_frames use MAX everywhere (transform pre-aggregated; re-MAX is harmless and consistent)."
